Subject: [PATCH] DeepSeek V4.1: select the opt-in Torch vision compatibility lane

Base: the imported Christopher Owen 1107 stack over Local Inference Lab vLLM
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, after the repository's recorded
patch series and after patch 0001 in this experiment.

Scope: add a local environment-controlled selector and a reference-style
per-image runner adapted from vLLM's existing non-packed DeepSeek image loop.
The default remains TileLang. The Torch lane requires data-parallel vision and
explicitly enables the arithmetic option introduced by 0001.

Provenance: the selector and factory adapters are newly implemented local
AI-assisted integration code.  The per-image runner is locally adapted and
refactored from upstream vLLM's existing non-packed DeepSeek image loop.  No
TensorFold source or binary is copied. The selector was already part of the
native compatibility deployment; this patch records it reproducibly and adds
the explicit tensorfold_compat_attention=True activation used by the audited
service.

Validation: original selector SHA256 ecf43fa91334ad768ee5c15386f939532cbfd734c8182a1494c8eb472fe640d0;
audited overlay SHA256 f4c899fde8117caaab1b18fc506389e0e504ce6cdb6c7ee19cad3100ba08c4d0.
Local experiment only; not represented as upstream-ready.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/vl_model.py | 71 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 69 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

